    "summary": "Textile (langtang) made of handspun cotton. Cloth has narrow warp-faced borders along each long side using thick natural-coloured and brown-dyed cotton arranged in alternating lines. The main part of the cloth is very loosely woven so that it appears net-like. The warp and weft use a combination of thin natural-coloured cotton and thicker brown-dyed cotton to form a pattern of warp and weft stripes.Long twisted cotton tassels at both ends.",
